creep finds vulnerabilities in local source code.

Usage:
  creep [global flags] <command> [flags] [args]

Commands:
  init     write ./creep.yaml: the project settings, each commented out at its default (ADR 0031)
  doctor   check the model (a command model must pass the tool canary) and the sandbox runtime
  scan     scan the repository in the current directory; reports go to .creep/
  estimate estimate the calls, tokens, time and cost of a scan here, without calling a model
  why      why <id>: show the evidence behind a finding of the last scan
  accept   accept <id> --expires 90d --reason "...": record a finding of the last scan as an accepted risk in the baseline file
  reproduce reproduce <id>: run a verified finding's PoC again from its bundle, in the sandbox, without a model
  clean    remove the containers, app images and networks creep left on local docker or podman, from any run
  resume   resume <run>: continue an interrupted run (checks the run; continuing it is not implemented yet)
  version  print version, commit and Go version
  config   explain: show each effective config value and the layer it came from
  bench    run creep-bench: the embedded corpus and its safe twins at tiers S, M and L, scored for recall, false positives and honesty per class; --replay reproduces the published numbers with no network (ADR 0030)
  mcp      serve the read-only MCP tools scan (changed files only), findings and why over stdio, for a coding agent (ADR 0027)
  recipe   new|lint|test <file.json>: write a recipe template, check a recipe, or load it by running its fixtures through the reader with your model (ADR 0025); add github.com/<owner>/<repo>@<commit> <clone>: install a source's recipes from your clone at that commit, pinned in creep.lock (ADR 0028)
  help     show this help

Global flags (before or after the command; "--" ends flags):
  --config <path>     config file used instead of the user and project files
  --model-run <cmd>   model CLI for contract command: prompt on stdin, JSON out
  --mode <mode>       scan: pr or nightly, which gate judges it (default pr, nightly
                      on a GitHub Actions schedule event); only nightly verifies
  --format <format>   output format: text, json, sarif, markdown (default "text")
  --log-level <level> log level: debug, info, warn, error (default "info")
  --record            call every model and record the responses for replay;
                      bench also writes the run's fixture file
  --replay            serve recorded responses only; never use the network;
                      bench serves its published fixture
  --recalibrate       calibrate the model again even if a calibration is cached
  --stats             scan: print phase times, model calls, cache hits and tokens
  --changed <file>    scan, estimate: only the paths listed in file, one per line or
                      NUL-separated (git diff --name-only -z origin/main > changed.txt);
                      every other source file is listed unchanged and not evaluated
  --stability <n>     scan, estimate: run discovery and every hypothesis n times (1 to
                      5, default 1); a finding seen in fewer runs is labeled an
                      unstable discovery
  --price-in <n>      estimate, --stats: price per 1M input tokens, for a cost
  --price-out <n>     estimate, --stats: price per 1M output tokens, for a cost
  --baseline <file>   scan: do not gate on findings the file's live entries match
                      (each still listed); accept: the file to write (default
                      creep-baseline.json)
  --baseline-write    scan: rewrite --baseline from this run's findings (a complete
                      run only); accepted risks are kept
  --expires <n>d      accept: days until the accepted risk expires (1d to 365d)
  --reason <text>     accept: why the risk is accepted (required)

Exit codes:
  0  nothing blocking
  1  gate exceeded
  2  usage or configuration error
  3  model or sandbox error
  4  incomplete run: report written, not everything evaluated
